hat $\\theta $ lies in $4$th quadrant. \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}=-\\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nThe principal value $\\theta $ is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ radians *clockwise* about the origin." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279425/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea036e3-19cd-572b-a6cb-2fa466c2a399"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279425"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170529/selection/b3fda50bbf7f6e23fc46ab50cb006ff963c382ad79f658273b8830b9eae26b11" :answer/id #uuid "3edd6f28-e83b-5056-909c-3cbe10d570c4" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055662/assets/efa0371723ca525e705c48e6ed2c741c95b1e68f6bce5d5aca0d52981290e6e5.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170529/selection/f13abce56ad739c4df1f69d6326b167c200fff11fc5c0f00e246718cb40e0a1e" :answer/id #uuid "2f061762-161b-5dac-94e7-fce554cf8810" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055662/assets/3a86f48c178d308b4a1301db6adee7b8ccf85a2603cf3e491e28ed8344971455.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170529/selection/74fffdb87aafe2766e83642956f8fe3dab109104841c1006ce0b63d71d1c4ad2" :answer/id #uuid "28eb9816-2c0c-5710-9e68-d4101a8bc932" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14055662/assets/20be1279911fea277028c369b374038b57899ea1e6c506f56b89bdc7780d73b9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170529/selection/f3c18f10f24dbbba0ae9881110f4b20cea9d138ae61e90f2bdf7863757cae75e" :answer/id #uuid "1e0adc85-88df-5505-8c9d-1e27c7662585" :answer/type :answer.t